# Example environment configuration

> Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values for your deployment. The keys are the same keys used by the DescribeAT PWA and the various backend services.

---

## Frontend (PWA) environment variables

These are read at build time by the PWA. See [`describeat-app`](https://gitlab.com/shazacin/describeat-app) for the full list.

```bash
# API endpoint (GraphQL)
VITE_API_ENDPOINT=https://api.example.com/graphql

# T2S endpoint (audio fingerprinting)
VITE_T2S_ENDPOINT=https://t2s.example.com/t2s/sync

# Media CDN base
VITE_MEDIA_CDN_BASE=https://media.example.com

# Auth provider
VITE_AUTH_PROVIDER=cognito
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-east-1_XXXXXXXXX
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=auth.example.com
VITE_COGNITO_REGION=us-east-1

# OAuth redirect URIs (must be registered in the auth provider)
VITE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=https://app.example.com/auth/callback
VITE_OAUTH_LOGOUT_URI=https://app.example.com

# Optional: Sentry / error tracking
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
```

## Backend (data layer) environment variables

```bash
# Database
DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/describeat

# Auth provider
COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-east-1_XXXXXXXXX
COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
COGNITO_REGION=us-east-1

# AWS (if using AppSync + DynamoDB)
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Storage
PUBLIC_BUCKET=describeat-public
PRIVATE_BUCKET=describeat-private
PUBLIC_BUCKET_REGION=us-east-1

# Notifications
FCM_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project
FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PATH=/secrets/firebase-service-account.json

# Logging
LOG_LEVEL=info
LOG_FORMAT=json
```

## Backend (fingerprinting engine) environment variables

```bash
# Matcher
MATCHER_PORT=5000
MATCHER_HASH_DB_PATH=/data/fingerprints
MATCHER_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.85
MATCHER_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Fingerprinter
FINGERPRINTER_PORT=5001
FINGERPRINTER_HASH_DB_PATH=/data/fingerprints
FINGERPRINTER_TRIGGER=s3-event
FINGERPRINTER_BUCKET=describeat-public
FINGERPRINTER_TRIGGER_PREFIX=ad-tracks/

# Storage
PRIVATE_BUCKET=describeat-private
PRIVATE_BUCKET_REGION=us-east-1
```

## What NOT to put in .env

Never put any of these in `.env`, `.env.production`, or any other environment file:

- Production database passwords (use Secrets Manager)
- API keys for third-party services (use Secrets Manager)
- OAuth client secrets (use Secrets Manager)
- FCM service account private key (use Secrets Manager)
- Cognito user pool admin credentials
- AWS root account credentials
- Any other secret

`.env` files are for non-secret configuration. For secrets, use a managed secret store.

## A note about `.env.example`

This file is `.env.example`. It is safe to commit. The values are placeholders. The actual `.env` file should NEVER be committed. Add `.env` to your `.gitignore`:

```
# .gitignore
.env
.env.local
.env.production
```
